      "message": "fix(tools): a short-flute meridian steps out to the full radius\n\nTool::meridian() ended a sharp taper or a drill at the cone top when the\nflute was shorter than the cone. Tool::profile() steps out to the full\nradius there. The ball nose and the bull nose had the same gap when the\nflute was shorter than the corner. The meridian now adds the radial\nshoulder (fl, r), as #3929 did for the flat and ball taper tips. The\nshoulder is a flat segment, so Meridian::atoms adds no atom and the\nsolid law pairing does not change. A tool whose flute reaches the full\nradius keeps the same meridian points.\n\nFixes #3938\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
